                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "41547676",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198057590719",
                            "num_reviews": 172,
                            "playtime_forever": 64,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 64,
                            "last_played": 1524077863
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Good: \nAesthetically, it is the best implementation of the game in VR. \nIt makes good use of VR and Vr really adds to the experience. \nIt has real potential if issues are addressed.\n\nThings that I would like to see (and the bad)\nThere seems to be no real challenge. What is there is fine for a sort of 'zen' mode and should be kept for that. \nBut it needs a harder mode with a timer - so you have a bit a of panic when up against the clock. \nWhen you have no more moves, the tiles are automatically shuffled - why? Isn't the the very idea of the game to think a strategy to avoid this and to take the correct tiles to solve the puzzle. Obviously, the stages would have to be worked out so that it is the players fault (rather than the game's) if you get the tiles locked. \nThe one thing that made it totally unplayable for me is when I found out that if you click a tile, the matching tile (if there is one) is highlighted. This removes the very last bit of challenge. All you really need to do is randomly click on tiles and let the game tell you where the matching tile is. \n\nPlease put me right if I have any of this wrong (and I will change the review) - or if there is an option I missed somewhere. I could not find one. \n\nSo, these issues make it pretty unplayable for me - I did not refund, as I want to support the development of the game and hope to see these issues addressed in a patch. If they are, I will change my negative into a positive and this will be then well worth the price being asked.  \n\nMy advice, hold up until it some of these gameplay issues are patched.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1524012214,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1524012214,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 3,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.503036379814148,
                        "comment_count": 2,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hi,  Thanks for the rich feedback.  We prefer to use the discussion pages instead of bad rating.  :)   We will change the \"help system\" at the next update, removing at the Medium and Hard difficulty.  Shuffle ... it's more problematic.  We have a large boards with more than 500 tiles. If we disabling the shuffle option, the user must follow in some cases the tile placing order.  But if you want I can add an option at the settings to disable the shuffle just for you :)   Our product been in Early Access for 5 months, we try to give a best.",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1524174370,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
                ],
